+### Discord
+
+Discord backend requires a bot token for authentication. Create an application
+in the [Discord Developer Portal](https://discord.com/developers/applications),
+add a bot to it, enable the **Message Content** privileged intent, and invite
+the bot to the server (guild) with only the **View Channels** and **Read
+Message History** permissions. The backend only reads; it never needs more.
+
+The backend fetches the messages of one channel or thread, given the guild
+(server) and channel identifiers. Enable Developer Mode in Discord to copy them
+with *Copy Server ID* and *Copy Channel ID*. Messages are fetched oldest first,
+so `--from-date` resumes a previous fetch, and the token is removed from the
+requests stored in an archive. A channel that does not belong to the given
+guild is refused.
+
+Each message keeps the `author` object Discord sends, including its `bot` flag,
+so messages written by bots can be told apart from those written by people.
+Perceval does not refetch messages edited or deleted after they were fetched;
+consider Discord's [Developer Policy](https://discord.com/developers/docs/policies-and-agreements/developer-policy)
+when storing them.
+
+```
+$ perceval discord 1301234567890123456 1301234567890123457 --from-date 2016-01-12 -t abcedefghijk
+```
+
